## Session 8 summary — real progress on the sole remaining gap (dir_reuse_coherency 32/caw)

**Criteria state: NOT yet met** — dir_reuse 32/caw is still the only gap (the status board confirmed 16/17 other 32/caw cells PASS). But I made concrete, validated progress by peeling two layered bugs:

**BUG 1 — round-5 shutdown → FIXED & PROVEN WORKING (0.10.57, build 78970C3C):**
- Root-caused via wall-clock (`realns`) correlation across all 32 nodes (the per-node dmesg clocks are unsynchronized — an early mis-read cost me a detour): a shared dir bmbt leaf, rewritten ~15× in 250ms by the current EX holder, is handed off fast; the next holder cold-reads it ~30ms later and gets a **transiently torn image** (bad CRC) from multipath/SCST-cache coherency lag → `xfs_trans_cancel` → shutdown → 0/32. A later raw dump of the same block was a valid leaf (torn state settled) → transient, not durable.
- **Fix:** bounded coherent re-read retry in `_xfs_buf_read` for multi-node dir metadata that fails read-verify CRC. **Validated live:** round 5 logged `P-DIRCRC-RETRY try=1 err=0 → RETRY-OK`, **0 shutdowns**, and the test progressed r1→r7 (vs. instant r5 shutdown on 0.10.56).

**BUG 2 — wedge#2, surfaced at round 7 once BUG 1 unblocked progress → FIX BUILT, UNTESTED (0.10.58):**
- rank1 `rm` hangs in `xfs_buf_iowait` (durable-signal bwrite) — a pre-existing lost-wakeup (sess5/6). `P-IOWAIT-STUCK sync_wait=0 ioend_seen=2` proved the sess6 `b_mxfs_sync_wait` snapshot races a lock-free XBF_ASYNC set (buf-item unpin on another CPU), so the completion mis-routes to the async/relse branch and never wakes the sync waiter.
- **Fix:** a `b_mxfs_force_sync` latch set under the buffer lock by sync submitters (`xfs_bwrite`, `_xfs_buf_read`) before submit — immune to the race — honored by `xfs_buf_submit`'s snapshot and completion-reinit.

**Next session** (details + exact commands in memory `AAA-ccloopa864-sess8-END-CRCfix-WORKS-wedge2-fix-built`): confirm build58, run `./run.sh 32 caw dir_reuse_coherency`, verify no `P-IOWAIT-STUCK`/shutdown and a full 32/32 PASS, then run 2–3× for stability before recording the criteria cell. Not writing YES — the fix chain isn't confirmed end-to-end yet.

